MODELS (downloaded on device or staged at demo time; not part of the source licence)
- Qwen3-0.6B (Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud), Apache-2.0. Used for offline narration
  and constrained field extraction.
- Laya multilingual 322M and Laya typed-decisions 421M (Convai Innovations),
  Apache-2.0. Used as a local classifier. Model card notes: shipped uncalibrated
  and over-confident; weak on some low-resource languages (Swahili 0.210 on
  MASSIVE); `noul` can under-report true. We therefore use two-option `choice`
  questions and never let the model's answer alone change the ledger.
- TranslatePsy-AfriSLM 0.8B (Tether AI Research), Apache-2.0. Used only to
  translate explanation text between English and Swahili, with numbers and
  entities masked before translation and verified afterwards. The model card
  states it is not validated for high-stakes or financial use; the app therefore
  never uses it for amounts, decisions, or advice.
- EasyOCR latin_g2 (Apache-2.0 upstream) and CRAFT detector (MIT upstream),
  converted to GGML by QVAC. Used only to read receipt photos on the phone.
- TiRex-2 is NOT bundled. If added later, its licence and weights must be
  recorded here before shipping.

DATA
- Kenyan public-holiday dates: compiled from public sources; provenance and
  verification status are recorded in packages/core/src/expect/holidays-ke.ts.
- Tariff tables: compiled from published Safaricom / M-PESA rate pages with
  retrieval dates in packages/core/src/tariffs/data/*.ts.
- No user data, customer data, or third-party private messages are included in
  this repository.
